Subject: [PATCH 0025] Pull frames from the interface thread

Pulling the frame inside the render pass ties the video to the interface: it
advances only when the interface repaints. The stream page underneath the stream
window is a still black backdrop, so there is nothing in it to redraw, and the
video rate follows whatever the interface happens to be doing instead of the
decoder.

The native side binds the thread that hands it the graphics device as its render
thread, and every frame has to be pulled from that thread. Nothing in this mode
touches the GPU, though: the decoder's DMA-BUF goes straight to the compositor,
and the compositor path never records into the command buffer it is handed. So
the device is handed over from the interface thread, which makes that thread the
one allowed to pull, and a timer there pulls and presents on a clock of its own.
The render pass only makes sure the pull is running.

Frame pacing is now the compositor's. On the reference board the same session
went from about 28 frames a second, limited by the interface, to the 54-55 that
the wire delivers, with nothing dropped.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STM32MP25 performance work]

